---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Special Relativity Cheat Sheet | Free Lorentz, Time Dilation, E=mc²"
  description="Complete special relativity cheat sheet with Lorentz transforms, time dilation, and E=mc². Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Special Relativity<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Lorentz transforms, time dilation, and E=mc². From postulates to applications.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Postulates</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Einstein's Postulates</h3>
        <pre><code>1. Laws of physics are the same in all inertial frames
2. Speed of light in vacuum is constant (c = 3 × 10⁸ m/s) for all observers</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Lorentz Transforms</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Coordinate Transforms</h3>
        <pre><code>x' = γ(x - vt)
t' = γ(t - vx/c²)
γ = 1/√(1 - v²/c²) (Lorentz factor)
Inverse&#58; swap primed/unprimed, change v to -v</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Velocity Addition</h3>
        <pre><code>u' = (u - v)/(1 - uv/c²)
Not simply u - v!
Always < c for any u, v < c</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Time Dilation & Length Contraction</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Time Dilation</h3>
        <pre><code>Δt' = γΔt (moving clocks run slow)
Δt₀&#58; proper time (rest frame)
Δt&#58; dilated time (moving frame)
Example&#58; μon lifetime extended</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Length Contraction</h3>
        <pre><code>L' = L₀/γ (moving objects shorter)
L₀&#58; proper length (rest frame)
L&#58; contracted length (moving frame)
Only along direction of motion</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Mass-Energy</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Energy-Momentum</h3>
        <pre><code>E = mc² (mass-energy equivalence)
E² = (pc)² + (m₀c²)²
p = γm₀v (relativistic momentum)
E_k = (γ - 1)m₀c² (kinetic energy)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
